Package: tufter
Type: Package
Title: Implement Edward Tufte's Principles of Graphical Design
Version: 0.6.4
Authors@R: person("Charles", "Crabtree",
                  email = "charles.crabtree@monash.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5144-8671"))
Description: Tools for drawing and reviewing statistical graphics with
    'ggplot2', based on Edward Tufte's ideas. Provides range frames, minimal
    box plots, dot plots, sparklines, slopegraphs, and direct series labels.
    Estimates data-ink ratio, lie factor, and data density, and checks colour
    contrast and label space. The audit reports explicit criteria separately
    from measurements without numerical targets, so results can be compared
    across drafts of a figure. For the underlying principles see Tufte
    (2001) "The Visual Display of Quantitative Information" (ISBN:0961392142),
    Tufte (1990) "Envisioning Information" (ISBN:0961392118), Tufte (1997)
    "Visual Explanations" (ISBN:0961392126), and Tufte (2006) "Beautiful
    Evidence" (ISBN:0961392177). For banking to 45 degrees see Cleveland,
    McGill and McGill (1988) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1988.10478598>.
